# ─── Rust build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Insta writes pending snapshots here while you review them. The reviewed
# `.snap` files next to them ARE committed: they are the expected output the
# transpiler tests assert against, and CI fails without them.
**/*.snap.new

# ─── OpenTaste local state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.taste/rules.json` is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the git-tracked,
# reviewable rule set and sharing it across the team is the point of the tool.
# Everything else under `.taste/` is a local cache that rescanning rebuilds.
.taste/cache.db
.taste/cache.db-wal
.taste/cache.db-shm
.taste/.lock
.taste/*.log

# ─── Node / TypeScript (phase 6: packages/) ───────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
out/
*.vsix
*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ─── Editor and agent scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent plan files are working notes, not project history.
.cursor/plans/
# `.cursor/rules/opentaste-*.mdc` and `.cursor/mcp.json` are intentionally left
# committable: they are what teammates who have not installed `taste` rely on.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
